rl":"https://www.kaggle.com"},"creator":{"@type":"sc:Person","name":"AJ","url":"/smayanj","image":"https://storage.googleapis.com/kaggle-avatars/thumbnails/15811302-kg.png?t=2025-02-22-08-55-10"},"publisher":{"@type":"sc:Organization","name":"Kaggle","url":"https://www.kaggle.com/organizations/kaggle","image":"https://storage.googleapis.com/kaggle-organizations/4/thumbnail.png"},"thumbnailUrl":"https://storage.googleapis.com/kaggle-datasets-images/7125175/11379903/f3006f8d8237cf8155eff103d5eb303b/dataset-card.png?t=2025-04-14-03-50-52","dateModified":"2025-04-12T16:35:18.613","datePublished":"2025-04-12T16:35:18.613","@type":"sc:Dataset","name":"Diabetes Risk Dataset","url":"https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/smayanj/diabetes-risk-dataset","description":"**Description:**  \nThis is a **synthetic health dataset** created to simulate individual medical and lifestyle profiles for predicting the risk of developing diabetes. It contains **12,000 rows**, where each row represents a unique person.\n\n---\n\n### Features:\n\n**age** - Person\u0027s age (between 20 and 80)\n**bmi** - Body Mass Index (normal distribution, clipped between 15 and 45)\n**glucose_level** - Blood glucose level (ranges from 60 to 200)\n **physical_activity_level** - Activity level: \u0060\u0027low\u0027\u0060, \u0060\u0027moderate\u0027\u0060, or \u0060\u0027high\u0027\u0060\n **family_history** - Binary (1 = yes, 0 = no). Indicates if diabetes runs in the family\n**smoker** - Binary (1 = yes, 0 = no). Whether the person is a smoker\n\n---\n\n### Target:\n\n- **at_risk_diabetes**  \n  Binary label (1 = high risk, 0 = low risk)  \n  Calculated using a rule-based model that weighs several factors:\n  - High BMI\n  - High glucose\n  - Older age\n  - Family history\n  - Smoking\n  - Low physical activity  \n  Random noise is added to make the prediction task more realistic.\n\n---\n\n**Use Cases:**  \nThis dataset is useful for:\n- Training classification models  \n- Building explainable AI tools for healthcare  \n- Practicing data analysis and visualization  \n- Simulating health screening tools in a safe, synthetic environment"}